# Both Directory stores: conflict, paging, expiry and request context

## Goal

Run the same public Directory contract against the Lab's two independent
repository algorithms, the instance-owned ETS store and the SQLite store
over Exqlite, and get the same answers from both: created and replaced
versions, exactly one winner among competing conditional writes, keyset
paging in a stable order, a cursor invalidated by a mutation, expiry after
the registration's TTL, and authorization decided by the request context
before any repository access. The SQLite store is then stopped and reopened
from its file with its entries and revision intact.

## Prerequisites

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:wotex_lab, "~> 0.1.0"},
  {:exqlite, "~> 0.40"}
])
```

The requirements above are published-artifact requirements. At the time this
notebook was written none of the `wotex*` packages is published on Hex; the
notebook is verified against the workspace source cohort recorded in
`priv/provenance/source-cohort.json` by `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_test.exs`,
which evaluates every Elixir cell below in order (skipping this install
cell). `Mix.install/1` never points at a Git checkout. The SQLite store
writes only under a temporary directory named in this notebook and removed
at the end.

## Package and consumer ownership

| Concern | Owner | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Directory operations, mutations, pages, cursors, expiry, errors, events | `wotex_directory` (package-implements) | `Wotex.Directory`, `Wotex.Directory.Service` |
| Repository storage (two algorithms) | `wotex_lab` (consumer-implements `Wotex.Directory.Repository`) | `Adapters.Directory.EtsRepository`, `SqliteRepository` |
| Authorization policy, clock, identifiers | `wotex_lab` (consumer-implements the three ports) | `Adapters.Directory.Authorization`, `Clock`, `Identifier` |
| Instance data directory and lifetime | consumer (this notebook) | `tmp_dir` and `Wotex.Lab.start_child/3` |

## Run

```elixir
alias Wotex.Directory
alias Wotex.Directory.{Context, Error, Expiry, Mutation, Page, Service}
alias Wotex.Lab
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.Directory.{Authorization, Clock, EtsRepository, Identifier, SqliteRepository}
alias Wotex.Lab.Telemetry
alias Wotex.ThingDescription

telemetry_id = "cookbook-directory-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

events =
  for component <- Telemetry.components(),
      operation <- Telemetry.operations(),
      event <- [:start, :stop, :exception],
      do: [:wotex, :lab, component, operation, event]

:ok = :telemetry.attach_many(telemetry_id, events, &Telemetry.forward/4, self())

fixture_dir = Application.app_dir(:wotex_lab, "priv/fixtures/directory")
{:ok, room} = fixture_dir |> Path.join("thing-description.json") |> File.read!() |> ThingDescription.parse()
{:ok, expected} = fixture_dir |> Path.join("expected-output.json") |> File.read!() |> Wotex.JSON.decode()
{:ok, start} = DateTime.from_iso8601(expected["clock"]) |> then(fn {:ok, at, _offset} -> {:ok, at} end)

thing = fn identifier, extra ->
  base = %{
    "@context" => Wotex.td_context_1_1(),
    "title" => "Lab Thing",
    "security" => ["nosec_sc"],
    "securityDefinitions" => %{"nosec_sc" => %{"scheme" => "nosec"}}
  }

  base = if identifier, do: Map.put(base, "id", identifier), else: base

  base =
    if Map.has_key?(extra, "registration"),
      do: Map.put(base, "@context", [Wotex.td_context_1_1(), "https://www.w3.org/2022/wot/discovery"]),
      else: base

  {:ok, td} = ThingDescription.from_map(Map.merge(base, extra))
  td
end

ThingDescription.id(room)
```

Both stores under one instance. The clock is an explicit agent that a cell
advances; identifiers are a counter; the policy for the first part allows
everything, which is confined to disposable simulations.

```elixir
{:ok, lab} = Lab.start_link(id: "directory", max_children: 8)
tmp_dir = Path.join(System.tmp_dir!(), "wotex-lab-cookbook-directory-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}")
File.mkdir_p!(tmp_dir)

{:ok, ets} = Lab.start_child(lab, :things, {EtsRepository, id: :ets})
{:ok, sqlite} = Lab.start_child(lab, :things, {SqliteRepository, id: :sqlite, path: tmp_dir})
{:ok, clock} = Clock.start_link(start)

service = fn module, repository, policy ->
  {:ok, identifier} = Identifier.start_link()

  {:ok, service} =
    Service.new(
      repository: {module, repository},
      authorization: {Authorization, policy},
      clock: {Clock, {:agent, clock}},
      identifier: {Identifier, identifier},
      introduction: room,
      default_page_limit: 2,
      max_page_limit: 4,
      default_expiry_batch_limit: 2,
      max_expiry_batch_limit: 4
    )

  {service, identifier}
end

context = Context.new!(:operator, repository: {:tenant, "room-1"})
stores = [{EtsRepository, ets}, {SqliteRepository, sqlite}]
```

One contract, run through the public `Wotex.Directory` functions against a
store, returning only statuses, versions, identifiers and error codes so the
two stores can be compared directly.

```elixir
exercise = fn module, repository ->
  {service, identifier} = service.(module, repository, :allow_all)
  store = module |> Module.split() |> List.last() |> String.replace_suffix("Repository", "") |> String.downcase()
  prefix = "urn:lab:#{store}"

  {:ok, %Mutation{status: created_status, entry: created}} = Directory.register(service, room, context)
  {:ok, %Mutation{status: replaced_status, entry: replaced}} = Directory.register(service, room, context)

  {:ok, %Mutation{status: patched_status, entry: patched}} =
    Directory.patch(service, ThingDescription.id(room), %{"title" => "Patched"}, context)

  {:ok, fetched} = Directory.get(service, ThingDescription.id(room), context)

  # Competing conditional replacements: exactly one wins.
  race_id = "#{prefix}:race"
  {:ok, %Mutation{entry: race}} = Directory.register(service, thing.(race_id, %{}), context)

  results =
    1..8
    |> Task.async_stream(fn n ->
      Directory.replace(service, race_id, thing.(race_id, %{"title" => "writer-#{n}"}), context,
        if_version: race.version
      )
    end)
    |> Enum.map(fn {:ok, result} -> result end)

  winners = Enum.count(results, &match?({:ok, _mutation}, &1))
  losers = Enum.count(results, &match?({:error, %Error{code: :conflict}}, &1))

  # Keyset paging in identifier order; one entry expires under a 30 s TTL.
  for suffix <- ["c", "a", "e", "b", "d"] do
    ttl = if suffix == "b", do: %{"registration" => %{"ttl" => 30}}, else: %{}
    {:ok, _mutation} = Directory.register(service, thing.("#{prefix}:list:#{suffix}", ttl), context)
  end

  {:ok, %Page{entries: page_one, next_cursor: cursor}} =
    Directory.list(service, Context.new!(:operator), limit: 2)

  Clock.advance(clock, 60)
  {:ok, %Page{entries: page_two, next_cursor: _cursor}} = Directory.list(service, context, cursor: cursor, limit: 3)
  {:ok, %Page{entries: fresh}} = Directory.list(service, context, limit: 4)
  {:ok, %Page{next_cursor: stale}} = Directory.list(service, context)
  {:ok, _mutation} = Directory.register(service, thing.("#{prefix}:list:f", %{}), context)
  {:error, %Error{code: stale_code}} = Directory.list(service, context, cursor: stale)

  # Expiry is bounded and repeatable: the room fixture (30 s TTL) and `b` are
  # due; retained entries answer `:expired`, a purge removes them.
  {:ok, %Expiry{strategy: retain, entries: retained}} = Directory.expire(service, context, strategy: :retain)
  {:error, %Error{code: expired_code}} = Directory.get(service, "#{prefix}:list:b", context)
  {:ok, %Expiry{strategy: purge, entries: purged}} = Directory.expire(service, context)
  {:ok, %Expiry{entries: nothing_left}} = Directory.expire(service, context)

  Agent.stop(identifier)

  %{
    "directory:register-created" => {created_status, created.version},
    "directory:register-replaced" => {replaced_status, replaced.version, patched_status, patched.version},
    "fetched-title" => ThingDescription.to_map(fetched.thing_description)["title"],
    "directory:conditional-conflict" => {winners, losers},
    "directory:page-order" =>
      {Enum.map(page_one, &String.replace(&1.identifier, prefix, "")),
       Enum.map(page_two, &String.replace(&1.identifier, prefix, ""))},
    "fresh-excludes-expired" => not Enum.any?(fresh, &String.ends_with?(&1.identifier, ":list:b")),
    "directory:cursor-invalidated" => stale_code,
    "directory:expired-after-ttl" => {retain, length(retained), expired_code, purge, length(purged), length(nothing_left)}
  }
end

outcomes = Map.new(stores, fn {module, repository} -> {module, exercise.(module, repository)} end)
outcomes[EtsRepository]
```

## Deliberate breakage

A scoped policy denies a stranger, a reader who tries to write, and a writer
with the wrong tenant, all before the repository sees a call. A broken policy
value is a typed authorization error, not a pass.

```elixir
policy = %{
  reader: [:get, :list],
  writer: {:tenant, "room-1", [:register, :get, :replace, :patch, :delete, :list, :expire]}
}

{scoped, scoped_identifier} = service.(EtsRepository, ets, policy)
insert_calls_before = Map.get(EtsRepository.stats(ets).calls, :insert, 0)

{:error, %Error{code: stranger_code}} =
  Directory.register(scoped, thing.("urn:wotex:lab:scoped:1", %{}), Context.new!(:stranger))

{:error, %Error{code: reader_code}} =
  Directory.register(scoped, thing.("urn:wotex:lab:scoped:1", %{}), Context.new!(:reader))

{:error, %Error{code: tenant_code}} =
  Directory.register(
    scoped,
    thing.("urn:wotex:lab:scoped:1", %{}),
    Context.new!(:writer, authorization: {:tenant, "room-2"})
  )

insert_calls_after = Map.get(EtsRepository.stats(ets).calls, :insert, 0)

{:ok, _mutation} =
  Directory.register(
    scoped,
    thing.("urn:wotex:lab:scoped:1", %{}),
    Context.new!(:writer, authorization: {:tenant, "room-1"})
  )

{broken, broken_identifier} = service.(EtsRepository, ets, :not_a_policy)
{:error, %Error{phase: broken_phase}} = Directory.get(broken, "urn:wotex:lab:scoped:1", Context.new!(:reader))
Agent.stop(scoped_identifier)
Agent.stop(broken_identifier)

{stranger_code, reader_code, tenant_code, insert_calls_before == insert_calls_after, broken_phase}
```

The SQLite store survives its owner: stop it, reopen the same file, and the
entries and the persisted collection revision are back. The ETS store is
volatile by design and starts empty after a restart.

```elixir
before = SqliteRepository.stats(sqlite)
file = SqliteRepository.database_path(sqlite)
:ok = GenServer.stop(sqlite)
{:ok, reopened} = SqliteRepository.start_link(path: tmp_dir)
after_reopen = SqliteRepository.stats(reopened)
{:ok, reopened_entry} = SqliteRepository.fetch(reopened, "urn:lab:sqlite:race", nil)
:ok = GenServer.stop(reopened)

sqlite_reopen? =
  File.exists?(file) and before.revision == after_reopen.revision and before.size == after_reopen.size and
    reopened_entry.version == 2

{before.revision, after_reopen.revision, before.size, sqlite_reopen?}
```

```elixir
:ok = Supervisor.stop(lab)
:ok = Agent.stop(clock)
{:ok, _removed} = File.rm_rf(tmp_dir)
```

## Safe telemetry

Directory spans label the repository operation and the store profile only;
identifiers, tenants and documents never become labels.

```elixir
drain = fn drain ->
  receive do
    {:wotex_lab_telemetry, event, measurements, metadata} ->
      [{event, measurements, metadata} | drain.(drain)]
  after
    0 -> []
  end
end

spans = drain.(drain)
:telemetry.detach(telemetry_id)

profiles =
  for {[:wotex, :lab, :directory, :directory, :stop], _measurements, metadata} <- spans,
      do: {metadata.profile, metadata.operation}

text = inspect(spans)
labels_safe? = not (text =~ "urn:wotex") and not (text =~ "room-1") and not (text =~ "Patched")
{Enum.uniq(profiles) |> Enum.sort(), labels_safe?}
```

## Expected output

| Check | Expectation |
| --- | --- |
| `both-stores-same-contract` | The outcome maps of the ETS and SQLite runs are equal |
| `conditional-conflict` | Eight competing replacements: 1 winner, 7 `:conflict` |
| `keyset-paging` | Page one is `a, b`; page two (limit 3) after the cursor is `c, d, e` and the expired `b` is gone from a fresh page |
| `cursor-invalidated` | A cursor issued before a registration is `:collection_changed` |
| `expiry` | The room fixture (30 s TTL) and `b` are retained as expired and read `:expired`; a purge removes both; the next batch is empty |
| `forbidden-context` | Stranger, reader and wrong tenant are `:forbidden` without a repository insert; a broken policy fails in the authorization phase |
| `sqlite-reopen` | The reopened file has the same revision and size, and the race entry is still version 2 |

```elixir
ets_outcomes = outcomes[EtsRepository]

%{
  "both-stores-same-contract" => ets_outcomes == outcomes[SqliteRepository],
  "conditional-conflict" => ets_outcomes["directory:conditional-conflict"] == {1, 7},
  "keyset-paging" =>
    ets_outcomes["directory:page-order"] == {[":list:a", ":list:b"], [":list:c", ":list:d", ":list:e"]} and
      ets_outcomes["fresh-excludes-expired"],
  "cursor-invalidated" => ets_outcomes["directory:cursor-invalidated"] == :collection_changed,
  "expiry" =>
    ets_outcomes["directory:expired-after-ttl"] == {:retain, 2, :expired, :purge, 2, 0} and
      ets_outcomes["directory:register-created"] == {:created, 1} and
      ets_outcomes["directory:register-replaced"] == {:replaced, 2, :patched, 3},
  "forbidden-context" =>
    {stranger_code, reader_code, tenant_code} == {:forbidden, :forbidden, :forbidden} and
      insert_calls_before == insert_calls_after and broken_phase == :authorization and labels_safe?,
  "sqlite-reopen" => sqlite_reopen?
}
```

## Public seam

`directory.repository` — `Wotex.Directory.Repository.fetch/3`, `insert/3`,
`replace/4`, `delete/4`, `list/5`, `expire_due/5` (consumer-implements; two
Lab references). `directory.authorization`, `directory.clock` and
`directory.identifier` (consumer-implements).

## Spec and completion IDs

* Lab: WLB.05 (`WLB-C05`, `WLB-C08`).
* Upstream consumer evidence: `WTD-C01`, `WTD-C02`, `WTD-C03`, `WTD-C04`.

## Replacement adapter

Implement `Wotex.Directory.Repository` over your database: `insert/3` must
be an atomic conditional create, `replace/4` and `delete/4` must apply their
version precondition inside the same unit of work, `list/5` must page by
identifier in code point order from the cursor, and the collection revision
must advance once per committed mutation. Run this notebook's `exercise`
function against your store next to the two references: equal outcome maps
are the contract.
